From f1a072dcd61dd11fac2b88e4c3472eeec0a895a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 21:24:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] block 10: k-quant-boosts - Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K/Q8_0 mmvq VDR decode, RDNA3_5 param table, mmq scale hoist, MoE whitelist

The single umbrella patch for k-quant and mmvq parameter work on RDNA
architectures. Q6_K VDR=2 (ex-block 09) and the gfx1151 mmvq parameter
table (ex-block 06) were folded in here so that excluding this one patch
restores 100% greedy-decoding purity across ALL architectures (RDNA3,
RDNA3_5, RDNA4) - all other blocks leave decode bit-identical within a
build:

- Q6_K mmvq VDR=2 decode kernel (formerly block 09, plus the
  GGML_CUDA_OP_TIMING graph-capture guard).
- Q4_K/Q5_K mmvq VDR=4 decode kernels (32 elements/thread, shared
  scale/d8 loads): decode n=1 -13%..-18% (q4_K) / -8%..-15% (q5_K).
- Q8_0 mmvq VDR=4 decode, RDNA4-gated (__GFX12__): -10%..-33% on the
  compute-bound shapes; other archs keep VDR=2 pending RDNA3/RDNA3_5
  verification.
- gfx1151 (RDNA3_5) mmvq parameter table (formerly block 06):
  MMVQ_PARAMETERS_RDNA3_5 split out of the RDNA2 fallback, nwarps=2 for
  Q8_0 decode (~+0.6% on Qwen3.6-35B-A3B Q8_0, swept 2025-08). Includes
  the verify-batch rule (ncols_dst 1..8) that block 10 used to carry.
- mmq prefill scale-load hoist in vec_dot_q8_1_q8_1_mma: q4_K n=16 -4.6%.
- RDNA4 MoE mmid whitelist Q4_K 4->7 (n=5/6/7 per expert -22%..-28%).
- perf harness: Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K/Q8_0 decode + prefill rows, MUL_MAT_ID
  bs=5/6/7.

Numerics (read before shipping): the VDR kernels reorder the fp32
cross-thread reduction, so compute outputs are not bit-identical to VDR=2
builds (max logit diff 0.184 vs flash-attn on/off's 0.203; greedy streams
are deterministic within a build but can flip across configs - 1 of 3 test
prompts diverged). PPL is unaffected (prefill path untouched): 6.3162/6.3563
on wikitext-2, matching the pre-block-12 records. If you require 100%
greedy purity across builds, do not apply this patch.

